Z||000000||nette||11-14-2001||11:56 AM||||Ok, three problems I need some help with.<P>1) Radiator fan is on ALL the time, as soon as you turn on the key.  Is this normal or is there a bad sensor or switch I don't know about?<P>2) Steering column problems<BR>a. brights switch doesn't work (no clicky)<BR>b. wipers only run on high speed - the other settings don't work<BR>c. the ignition is weird, it doesn't seem to have an accessory setting (should it?) and if you turn it slowly you can get the radio to come on without all the idiot lights on the dash coming on<P>3) 2.5 4 cyl has blow-by and is getting tired.  Options are to purchase a replacement motor or have this one rebuilt.  The replacement (if I go 4 cyl) will run about 2k, the rebuild will run about 3k.  Any suggestions?  Should I stick with the 4 cyl or go with a 6 cyl?<P>Any help on these problems would be greatly appreciated.  Happy Thanksgiving!<P>nette||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||11-14-2001||01:24 PM||||#1) Fan has been hot wired. That circuit needs to be trouble shot to locate the problem, repaired and the jumper removed.<P>#2 part a) Check and see if the rod that is visible on the column about half way down is seated into the dimmer switch. It should rest in a small cup on the switch.<BR>b) Hard to say without knowing the history. A couple of things come to mind. 1-someone replaced the switch, someone replaced the wiper motor or someone replaced the stalk. I would suspect the switch or the stalk because of the trouble with the dimmer switch.<BR>c) There should be an Acc. position just like everything else. Sounds like the column has been monkeyed with. <BR>(No offense Monkeyman!)<P>3) Your call on that one. Your wallet, not mine.||||reg||1
